1
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,600
I don't want you to go anywhere.

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,066
You're so unfair.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,800
I was actually to let you go.

4
00:00:15,466 --> 00:00:16,266
Why are you looking at me?

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,300
Because you're cute.

6
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,333
Woof-woof.

7
00:00:18,466 --> 00:00:19,266
Book.

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,500
Are you starting to like me yet?

9
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,333
I'll give in to you just for today.

10
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,400
I'm exhausted.

11
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,400
Me too.

12
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,166
But I think it's great.

13
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:31,700
Really great.

14
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:49,500
Hey.

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,966
Can I sleep over at your house?

16
00:00:53,166 --> 00:00:53,966
Sleep over?

17
00:00:54,466 --> 00:00:55,966
You should go back and sleep at your house.

18
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:58,100
It's my house.

19
00:00:58,333 --> 00:00:59,200
I've already slept there.

20
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:01,133
But at your house--

21
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,333
You already slept at my house before.

22
00:01:02,866 --> 00:01:03,766
You should go back.

23
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,000
Can I sleep over at your place?

24
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,533
Can I?

25
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:11,466
What are you doing?

26
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,566
Hello, Jie Fing.

27
00:01:15,566 --> 00:01:16,900
It's late now.

28
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:19,933
Can I sleep over at your place?

29
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,300
Um.

30
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:22,500
Of course.

31
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:23,600
Come on in.

32
00:01:23,933 --> 00:01:24,800
Hey, Jie.

33
00:01:25,266 --> 00:01:26,066
Thank you.

34
00:03:04,738 --> 00:03:05,796
Um.

35
00:03:05,796 --> 00:03:07,266
(Ma) You can't do it like that.
(Pa) Why does it always go too far?

36
00:03:07,266 --> 00:03:09,536
Are you gonna say that's beacuse you're too good?

37
00:03:09,572 --> 00:03:10,492
Yeah, absolutely.

38
00:03:10,492 --> 00:03:12,492
Why do you trim the head off?

39
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,694
Pa, Ma, I'm back.

40
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:16,811
You're back.

41
00:03:16,811 --> 00:03:17,682
Hello.

42
00:03:17,683 --> 00:03:18,456
Hello.

43
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:26,533
I really miss you.

44
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,733
Tee, you can join us.

45
00:03:29,733 --> 00:03:30,533
Okay.

46
00:03:32,066 --> 00:03:33,066
Alright, we're complete.

47
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,500
You take advantage of the situation.

48
00:03:44,797 --> 00:03:45,933
I miss you, honey.

49
00:03:46,566 --> 00:03:47,533
How was your day? Is it tired?

50
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,200
Whoa, you see right through me.

51
00:03:52,066 --> 00:03:54,200
Does anyone want to give me a hand
with these bean sprouts?

52
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:55,166
Nah.

53
00:03:55,166 --> 00:03:56,500
Does no one want to help me?

54
00:03:56,566 --> 00:03:57,800
It's all yours.

55
00:04:02,266 --> 00:04:03,533
I'll help you.

56
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,300
Help me?

57
00:04:06,866 --> 00:04:07,906
Yes, help you with these bean sprouts.

58
00:04:07,906 --> 00:04:08,800
Hmm?

59
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,600
May I help you?

60
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,400
Wow.

61
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:27,300
He can really do it.

62
00:04:27,733 --> 00:04:28,533
He even does it smoothly.

63
00:04:28,866 --> 00:04:29,666
Pa, look.

64
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,200
(Ma) So, you like eating bean sprouts.
(Pa) I'd better do something else.

65
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:33,500
Oh.

66
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:35,766
Where are you going?

67
00:04:35,966 --> 00:04:36,766
Wow, you're leaving.

68
00:04:36,856 --> 00:04:37,356
I'm leaving.

69
00:04:40,939 --> 00:04:42,153
Tee, do you like bean sprouts?

70
00:04:42,730 --> 00:04:43,230
I like them.

71
00:04:43,707 --> 00:04:45,658
I'd better fix a floor lamp. It keeps flickering.

72
00:04:46,401 --> 00:04:47,599
Excuse me.

73
00:04:47,601 --> 00:04:48,384
Yes.

74
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,101
I'll help you.

75
00:04:51,794 --> 00:04:52,420
Huh?

76
00:04:53,234 --> 00:04:53,860
Can you fix it?

77
00:04:54,351 --> 00:04:55,026
I can.

78
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,321
So talented.

79
00:04:58,321 --> 00:05:00,300
You can do anything from trimming
bean sprouts to fixing the lamp.

80
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:01,966
Thanks, thanks.

81
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:03,630
Um.

82
00:05:04,906 --> 00:05:06,238
Let me help you.

83
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,698
Thank you, Tee.

84
00:05:10,698 --> 00:05:13,455
You're the best.

85
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,766
Tee, you're so nice.

86
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,100
Thanks for saying that.

87
00:05:18,666 --> 00:05:20,466
Unlike a kid around here.

88
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,000
Huh?

89
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,900
Huh? Look, he's helping us.

90
00:05:29,966 --> 00:05:32,866
Well, would you consider me your son?

91
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:37,933
Why not?

92
00:05:38,666 --> 00:05:41,700
I want to have a good-looking son
like you for a long time.

93
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,500
I'm good-looking too, right?

94
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:47,926
Yeah, you're good-looking.

95
00:05:48,122 --> 00:05:50,178
My lil monkey.

96
00:05:51,896 --> 00:05:53,113
But Tee is more good-looking.

97
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,266
But I think... Papa is the most good-looking.

98
00:05:59,503 --> 00:06:00,374
Aww.

99
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,200
Now you're talking.

100
00:06:03,466 --> 00:06:05,600
You can stay with me as long as you want.

101
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:06,766
Can he be your son?

102
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,933
Hold on.

103
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:12,892
Take him to the kitchen. I want to see
whether he can prep ingredients or not.

104
00:06:12,892 --> 00:06:14,500
If he can, I'll accept him as my son.

105
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,200
Really?

106
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:15,796
Yeah.

107
00:06:15,796 --> 00:06:16,766
Let's head over.

108
00:06:17,166 --> 00:06:18,028
Go, go.

109
00:06:18,028 --> 00:06:18,800
Come over here.

110
00:06:18,966 --> 00:06:19,900
Will you accept him as our son?

111
00:06:20,366 --> 00:06:21,533
Well, let's see.

112
00:06:21,866 --> 00:06:23,200
Let's go.

113
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:27,933
Fuse.

114
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:34,200
I'd better go see Tee.

115
00:06:35,921 --> 00:06:38,854
Tee~

116
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,708
Tee!

117
00:06:44,641 --> 00:06:45,966
You're being extra.

118
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:22,100
Wow. You look good from every angle,
like me in my old days.

119
00:07:23,766 --> 00:07:25,108
Do you think he's as handsome as you?

120
00:07:25,108 --> 00:07:25,834
Um.

121
00:07:25,834 --> 00:07:26,400
Like you in your old days?

122
00:07:26,666 --> 00:07:27,533
Yeah, like looking in the mirror.

123
00:07:27,866 --> 00:07:29,261
I can't remember that.

124
00:07:29,261 --> 00:07:29,761
Eh?

125
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,100
Hmph.

126
00:07:31,133 --> 00:07:31,933
You...

127
00:07:32,133 --> 00:07:33,733
You used to compliment me.

128
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,300
Now, you're getting old and...

129
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:37,100
starting to lose your memories.

130
00:07:37,766 --> 00:07:39,366
Hey, come on.

131
00:07:39,533 --> 00:07:41,666
How could you forget how handsome I am?

132
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,500
It's like looking in the mirror.

133
00:07:43,733 --> 00:07:44,905
Okay, go back to your seat.

134
00:07:44,905 --> 00:07:45,405
Hmm?

135
00:07:45,405 --> 00:07:48,133
What do you mean I'm losing my memories?
Fuse, go back to your seat.

136
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:51,855
Back to your seat.

137
00:07:52,542 --> 00:07:53,321
Come over here.

138
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:57,667
By the way...

139
00:07:58,158 --> 00:07:59,914
You're really handsome, Tee.

140
00:08:00,356 --> 00:08:01,502
With a face like that,

141
00:08:01,993 --> 00:08:04,103
girls must be all over you, right?

142
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:05,477
Tee.

143
00:08:06,115 --> 00:08:06,950
Are you dating anyone?

144
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,515
Ma.

145
00:08:13,104 --> 00:08:16,237
Gen Z doesn't just become
a couple easily these days.

146
00:08:16,581 --> 00:08:19,844
They have to pass a
talking stage before becoming a couple.

147
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,900
They're a couple, but they define
themselves as being in the talking stage?

148
00:08:23,266 --> 00:08:25,100
Not a couple, they just seeing each other.

149
00:08:27,066 --> 00:08:30,189
Wait, in that case...

150
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:31,796
that's called leading someone on.

151
00:08:31,866 --> 00:08:32,666
Yeah.

152
00:08:32,766 --> 00:08:35,256
If they refuse to use the word "couple"...

153
00:08:35,256 --> 00:08:37,982
and play the field,

154
00:08:37,982 --> 00:08:39,521
that means they keep their
options open to see what works.

155
00:08:39,521 --> 00:08:42,166
Is that right, Tee?

156
00:08:42,366 --> 00:08:43,166
Hmm?

157
00:08:45,766 --> 00:08:46,794
I feel like...

158
00:08:47,628 --> 00:08:48,832
If I like someone,

159
00:08:49,372 --> 00:08:50,745
I only have eyes for them.

160
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,066
There you go.

161
00:08:55,557 --> 00:08:56,424
Ma, you see?

162
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:58,333
Besides being handsome,

163
00:08:59,118 --> 00:09:01,201
he's as faithful and loyal as I am.

164
00:09:01,482 --> 00:09:02,575
Um.

165
00:09:02,575 --> 00:09:03,495
That's so sweet.

166
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:05,128
Look at your dad.

167
00:09:05,129 --> 00:09:08,552
He suddenly turned
the conversation back to himself.

168
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:17,593
Ma, fight back. Don't let him win.

169
00:09:17,826 --> 00:09:19,300
Nah.

170
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:19,800
Tee.

171
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:20,500
Yes?

172
00:09:20,766 --> 00:09:21,800
I'll tell you what.

173
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:24,000
If our family goes on a trip,

174
00:09:24,266 --> 00:09:26,933
you must come with us. Okay?

175
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:27,733
Sure.

176
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,766
Let's eat.

177
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,133
Here are the bean sprouts that Tee had trimmed.

178
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:37,066
Alright.

179
00:09:37,066 --> 00:09:38,466
It's time to eat.

180
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,400
Tee.

181
00:10:30,066 --> 00:10:31,400
What is that on your shirt?

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,566
Well, I went to help Pa carry a flower pot.

183
00:10:35,666 --> 00:10:36,668
I see.

184
00:10:37,699 --> 00:10:39,266
You're serving my dad too much.

185
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:41,666
Your dad can't carry it by himself.

186
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:45,949
That's true.

187
00:10:47,422 --> 00:10:49,955
The bathroom is free. Go take a shower before Jie.

188
00:10:50,593 --> 00:10:51,466
Or you'll have to wait for a long time.

189
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,100
Take it.

190
00:11:18,666 --> 00:11:19,996
(Jeen) Are you home now?

191
00:11:20,683 --> 00:11:22,000
(Jeen) I'm still at Siam.

192
00:11:22,666 --> 00:11:23,610
You've been there so long.

193
00:11:24,837 --> 00:11:25,766
Who are you with?

194
00:11:26,533 --> 00:11:27,984
I... I'm with my friend.

195
00:11:28,818 --> 00:11:30,666
Well, did you and Tee
go seperate ways heading home?

196
00:11:31,066 --> 00:11:31,866
Why?

197
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:33,632
Well...

198
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:35,533
Just in case we hang out with him again.

199
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:37,852
I think...

200
00:11:37,852 --> 00:11:40,007
I might invite my friend next time.

201
00:11:40,498 --> 00:11:41,904
So it'll be a double date.

202
00:11:42,297 --> 00:11:45,806
My friend is cute, and she has a lot of followers.

203
00:11:45,806 --> 00:11:47,557
I think Tee will like her.

204
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:49,326
This is mine.

205
00:11:49,326 --> 00:11:50,648
And yours is...

206
00:11:50,648 --> 00:11:51,148
This one.

207
00:11:53,066 --> 00:11:53,900
Which one is better?

208
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,200
The red one.

209
00:12:00,933 --> 00:12:01,741
Look.

210
00:12:03,263 --> 00:12:04,234
Jeen.

211
00:12:06,786 --> 00:12:08,166
I need to talk to you.

212
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:11,266
I have to go now. I'll let you know
when I'm at home. Bye.

213
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:12,533
Hey.

214
00:13:04,675 --> 00:13:05,952
I only like you.

215
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:11,108
But I understand that…

216
00:13:13,226 --> 00:13:14,118
it's impossible for us.

217
00:13:52,282 --> 00:13:53,482
Can you dry my hair?

218
00:13:54,315 --> 00:13:55,182
Who are you asking me to do that?

219
00:13:56,848 --> 00:13:57,817
I'll be anything...

220
00:13:58,308 --> 00:13:59,729
you want me to be.

221
00:14:02,848 --> 00:14:03,648
Fine.

222
00:14:07,182 --> 00:14:07,982
Turn around.

223
00:14:28,848 --> 00:14:30,882
Ouch, that's too hard.

224
00:14:32,448 --> 00:14:34,315
Oh, sorry.

225
00:14:38,882 --> 00:14:39,848
You're just messing with me.

226
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:51,140
Tee.

227
00:14:51,435 --> 00:14:53,143
Why do you have such broad shoulders?

228
00:14:54,715 --> 00:14:55,515
Do you like them?

229
00:14:57,782 --> 00:14:59,715
Nah, I didn't say that.

230
00:15:00,515 --> 00:15:01,482
So you don't like them?

231
00:15:08,515 --> 00:15:10,548
You don't have to answer. I'm just joking around.

232
00:15:44,182 --> 00:15:45,915
Oh, he posted the pictures.

233
00:15:46,282 --> 00:15:47,082
Wait, let me see.

234
00:15:51,848 --> 00:15:54,282
Whoa, he also posted my pic.

235
00:16:01,915 --> 00:16:02,715
Hey.

236
00:16:03,748 --> 00:16:05,482
Why don't you keep your pics?

237
00:16:08,982 --> 00:16:10,482
I don't want to keep mine.

238
00:16:11,548 --> 00:16:12,748
I want to keep ours.

239
00:16:35,682 --> 00:16:36,482
Stop it.

240
00:17:09,582 --> 00:17:11,748
Did she just call?

241
00:17:16,848 --> 00:17:17,948
Do you mean Jeen?

242
00:17:19,548 --> 00:17:20,348
Um.

243
00:17:26,082 --> 00:17:27,748
She wants to invite you to go out.

244
00:17:31,982 --> 00:17:34,011
So she could introduce her friend to you.

245
00:17:37,005 --> 00:17:38,316
Her friend is cute, though.

246
00:17:39,690 --> 00:17:42,182
She has a lot of followers, just in case you like it.

247
00:18:03,682 --> 00:18:04,882
I only like you.

248
00:18:09,115 --> 00:18:10,310
But I understand that...

249
00:18:12,126 --> 00:18:13,282
it's impossible for us.

250
00:18:52,848 --> 00:18:54,048
I feel uncomfortable.

251
00:18:57,315 --> 00:18:58,292
I'm uncomfortable that...

252
00:18:59,715 --> 00:19:01,262
I don't know what should I do.

253
00:19:12,682 --> 00:19:14,115
What do you want to do the most, then?

254
00:19:20,848 --> 00:19:21,876
I want to be with you.

255
00:19:24,085 --> 00:19:25,384
Right here.

256
00:19:34,782 --> 00:19:35,948
Why not?

257
00:19:55,115 --> 00:19:56,115
I'm here.

258
00:21:27,303 --> 00:21:29,303
[What are you guys doing tonight?]

259
00:21:32,598 --> 00:21:33,237
[What are you guys doing tonight?]

260
00:21:33,237 --> 00:21:34,008
[That's cute.]

261
00:21:34,008 --> 00:21:34,668
[Whose fortune is this?]

262
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:35,439
[Answer my DM, please.]

263
00:21:35,439 --> 00:21:36,210
[Won't your partner be jealous of posting this pic?]

264
00:21:36,210 --> 00:21:37,515
[Aren't you cold? I can give you a hug.]

265
00:22:08,914 --> 00:22:15,086
[Delete it.]

266
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:21,650
[Stop it, or I'll block you.]

267
00:22:24,201 --> 00:22:26,201
[Loudly crying face emojis]

268
00:22:38,044 --> 00:22:40,044
[Others can only look, but you already touched it.
Isn't that enough?]

269
00:22:40,535 --> 00:22:42,535
[Skull emojis]

270
00:23:14,315 --> 00:23:15,548
Hurry up, everybody.

271
00:23:15,882 --> 00:23:16,682
Hurry up.

272
00:23:19,048 --> 00:23:19,702
Alright.

273
00:23:19,702 --> 00:23:21,582
Hurry up.

274
00:23:21,948 --> 00:23:23,882
Did I leave my bag?

275
00:23:30,248 --> 00:23:30,770
Where are you going?

276
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:31,648
What?

277
00:23:31,948 --> 00:23:33,882
I already told you guys yesterday.

278
00:23:34,048 --> 00:23:35,748
You talked about a lot of things yesterday.

279
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,048
Hmm?

280
00:23:37,948 --> 00:23:39,848
I mean about our trip.

281
00:23:40,248 --> 00:23:41,848
Tee already agreed to go on a trip together.

282
00:23:42,048 --> 00:23:42,848
Hmm?

283
00:23:43,915 --> 00:23:46,048
